# Catalogue

Editorial strings use `L10nText` (`en` required; any other locale key optional). Resolve `locale → en → first key`. Chrome copy (Play, Settings) belongs in i18next, not the catalogue. Validate JSON with Valibot in `src/catalogue/schema.ts`.

Host: Cloudflare Pages Direct Upload from `Open-Sikh-Apps/gurbani-paath-player-catalogue` (Wrangler CI, not Connect-to-Git). Probe `catalogue.version.json`, then `catalogue.json?v={version}` on mismatch. Catalogue repo CI checkouts this app, fills missing `byteSize` via HEAD (`scripts/fill-catalogue-bytesize.ts`), then Valibot (`npx tsx scripts/validate-catalogue.ts`) before upload. On device: off-thread `JSON.parse` plus a cheap shape check; persist the downloaded text in MMKV (`id: "catalogue"`, `format` key). Do not run full Valibot on device. Refresh on cold start, Home pull-to-refresh, and Home overflow — not on `AppState` `active`, and not when Android remounts `RootLayout` from a notification tap (`catalogueReady` in `src/app/_layout.tsx` skips that fetch). `EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK_CATALOGUE` (`1` / `true` / `yes`) uses only bundled `mock-catalogue.json` and skips Pages plus disk cache; it is not tied to `__DEV__`. The app never calls Sanity. GitHub-edited `catalogue.json` is enough for V1.

```ts
type L10nText = { en: string; [locale: string]: string };
type L10nUrl = { en: string; [locale: string]: string };
type ThemedMediaUrl =
  | string
  | { light: string; dark: string };

type Author = {
  id: string;
  name: L10nText;
  imageUrl?: ThemedMediaUrl;
  aboutUrl?: L10nUrl;
};

type Reciter = {
  id: string;
  name: L10nText;
  imageUrl?: ThemedMediaUrl;
  aboutUrl?: L10nUrl;
};

type Scripture = {
  id: string;
  name: L10nText;
  imageUrl?: ThemedMediaUrl; // `/images/…` or https; `{ light, dark }` when both exist
  aboutUrl?: L10nUrl;
  sttmCoSlug?: string; // https://sttm.co/{sttmCoSlug}/{startAng}
};

type ResourceSection = {
  id: string;
  title: L10nText;
};

type ResourceItem = {
  id: string;
  sectionId: string; // ResourceSection.id
  title: L10nText;
  description: L10nText;
  url: string;
};

type TrackBase = {
  id: string;
  title: L10nText;
  url: string; // `/audio/{collectionId}/{trackId}.mp3` or absolute https; app prepends EXPO_PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL for paths
};

type SehajPaathTrack = TrackBase & {
  kind: "sehaj_paath";
  durationSec: number;
  byteSize: number; // R2 object Content-Length; ≤ 512 MiB
  startAng?: number;
  endAng?: number;
  angTimestamps?: { tSec: number; ang: number }[];
};

type AudiobookTrack = TrackBase & {
  kind: "audiobook";
  durationSec: number;
  byteSize: number; // R2 object Content-Length; ≤ 512 MiB
  readAlongUrl?: string;
};

type RadioTrack = TrackBase & {
  kind: "radio";
};

type Track = SehajPaathTrack | AudiobookTrack | RadioTrack;

type CollectionBase = {
  id: string;
  title?: L10nText;
  authorId?: string;
  languages: string[];
  artworkUrl?: ThemedMediaUrl;
  downloadable: boolean;
};

type SehajPaathCollection = CollectionBase & {
  kind: "sehaj_paath";
  reciterId: string;
  scriptureId: string;
  tracks: SehajPaathTrack[];
};

type AudiobookCollection = CollectionBase & {
  kind: "audiobook";
  reciterId?: string;
  scriptureId?: string;
  tracks: AudiobookTrack[];
};

type RadioCollection = CollectionBase & {
  kind: "radio";
  reciterId?: string;
  scriptureId?: string;
  tracks: RadioTrack[];
};

type Collection = SehajPaathCollection | AudiobookCollection | RadioCollection;

type Catalogue = {
  version: number;
  heroImageUrl: ThemedMediaUrl;
  authors: Author[];
  reciters: Reciter[];
  scriptures: Scripture[];
  collections: Collection[];
  resourceSections: ResourceSection[];
  resources: ResourceItem[];
};
```

Every `id` (Author, Reciter, Scripture, Collection, Track, ResourceSection, ResourceItem) must be unique across the whole catalogue. Prefer UUID.

`durationSec` and `byteSize` are required on `sehaj_paath` and `audiobook` tracks. `byteSize` is the stored object’s Content-Length (catalogue CI HEADs the URL if omitted; do not guess from bitrate). Radio tracks omit both — live streams have no finite length or file size.

V1 Home lists `kind === "sehaj_paath"` only, grouped by `scriptureId` (scripture title + image), then reciter-named collections. `sehaj_paath` requires `reciterId` and `scriptureId`. Keep `kind` / `languages` / `scriptureId` for later filters. Group Resources by `sectionId` → `ResourceSection`.
